 "_doc": "Our own props in this zone. walls (E9b1; OwnWalls.cs): pieces maps a KayKit village piece of props.json to our presets (tools/assets/env_house.json, art/world/house) as treatments: a house takes the list of its treatment (houses: \"<h>\": [plaster tint 0-5, treatment 0 plain / 1 crosses / 2 braces], written by tools/godot/house_ids.py so neighbors differ), each copy one of that list by its place; an empty list drops the kit piece (its window glass, door frame or door is in our wall piece). Roofs (E9b2; tools/assets/env_roof.py): the roof bodies, spires and chimneys named in \"by_roof\" take the list of their house's roof covering (houses' third number: 0 clay pantiles, 1 oak shingles; the fourth its tint), the gable fronts the list of its treatment like the walls. (E9d) place: the square's own stalls, notice board and the market's clutter (env_props.json), the web game's stalls and board hidden; clear: [x, z, r] where the kit's wares and stock at the stalls go. (E9d r2) col: [cx, cz, hw, hd], a place's box collider in its preset's frame (ZoneMeta.AddPropColliders); braziers: ours over the web game's stand. (Env 22 r1f) night_lamps: lamps of the zone's own where the night left a dead zone (ZoneView.Town.NightLamps): holder (lamps.json kind), on [x, z, rot] (the piece it stands on), local [x, y, z] in that piece's frame (y over the ground), turn, color, energy, range, att, spec, scale; each its own unshadowed light, cold by day.",
